      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, my dear friend, let me tell you a tale of the wise old goblin, Salty the Salt, who once lived in the mystical land of Cryptonia. Salty the Salt knew that even the most powerful of goblin spells, like the mighty SHA-256, could be tricked by the sneaky goblins known as Rainbow Tables. These tables, crafted by goblin wizards, could quickly reverse-engineer the scrambled passwords if they were not properly guarded.\n\nSo, Salty the Salt devised a clever trick: he sprinkled a unique, random goblin dust, known as a \"salt,\" onto the password before scrambling it with SHA-256. This salt ensured that even if two goblins tried to use the same spell, the resulting scrambled password would be as different as night and day, thanks to the unique salt. This way, the goblins couldn't use their Rainbow Tables to easily reverse-engineer the passwords, keeping the treasure trove of secrets safe from prying eyes.\n\nAnd so, my friend, adding a salt to your password before hashing it is like giving your password a magical shield, making it even harder for those pesky goblins to crack your code. Remember, in the world of security, it's always",
