      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes sense. \n\nbut i have one more question about how it's actually stored. if the salt is stored in the same database right next to the hash, doesn't that just mean an attacker who breaches the DB has everything they need to just start building those new tables for each salt? wouldn't that defeat the whole point?",
      "source": "evaluator"
